{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"2c52cb85-cc14-49e1-a8da-78dc99b1e03e","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A tangent touches a circle at exactly one point. Call that point T, and call the centre O.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Radius meets tangent"},{"op":"figure","id":"circlefig","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-3.2,3.2],"y":[-2.6,3]},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"centre","at":[0,0],"label":"O"},{"kind":"circle","id":"circle","center":{"at":"centre"},"r":2},{"kind":"point","id":"touch","at":[0,2],"label":"T"},{"kind":"segment","id":"tangent","from":[-2.8,2],"to":[2.8,2],"label":"tangent"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"2c52cb85-cc14-49e1-a8da-78dc99b1e03e","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Draw the radius from O to T. The radius and tangent meet at a right angle.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"radiusadd","on":"circlefig","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"radius","from":{"at":"centre"},"to":{"at":"touch"}},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"touch"},"from":{"at":"centre"},"to":[2,2],"label":"90°"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"OT\\perp\\text{tangent at }T"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"2c52cb85-cc14-49e1-a8da-78dc99b1e03e","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Why? T is the closest point on the tangent to O. Every other point lies outside the circle, farther than one radius away.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"compare","on":"circlefig","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"other","at":[2,2],"label":"P"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"centre"},"to":{"at":"other"},"stroke":"dashed"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"distance","anchor":{"el":"rule","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"OP>OT=r"},{"op":"text","id":"reason","anchor":{"el":"distance","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"Shortest distance to a line is perpendicular."}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"2c52cb85-cc14-49e1-a8da-78dc99b1e03e","step":{"id":"s4","script":"So whenever you see a tangent, join the centre to the touching point and mark a right angle.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"emphasis","on":"circlefig","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[-1.05,0.95],"text":"radius","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"answer","anchor":{"el":"reason","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\angle OTP=90^\\circ"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What angle does a tangent make with the radius at the point of contact?","expected_gist":"90 degrees, a right angle"}}}
